                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_06\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes AbstractElement.equals() in\ntitan-core/src/main/java/com/thinkaurelius/titan/graphdb/internal/AbstractElement.java\nfrom:\n    return getId().equals(((TitanVertex)other).getId());\n    return getId().equals(((TitanEdge)other).getId());\nback to:\n    return getID() == ((TitanVertex)other).getID();\n    return getID() == ((TitanEdge)other).getID();\n\nThe fix commit message explicitly states the intent: \"Call AbstractElement\ngetID() insteado of getId()\", explaining that relying on capitalization\n(getID vs getId) to differentiate methods is error-prone.\n\ncandidate_06's diff shows the equals() method being rewritten from an\nif/else-if block that used `getID()==((AbstractElement)other).getID()`\n(a single combined check) into the current structure that split it into\nseparate TitanVertex/TitanEdge branches AND, critically, switched from the\n`getID()` long-comparison to `getId().equals(...)`. This is precisely the\nbuggy code pattern that the fix commit reverts.\n\ncandidate_07's diff exactly matches the fix commit's diff (same blob hashes\n339f4a0..ca0bb90), confirming candidate_07 is the fix commit itself, and\ncandidate_06 (blob 8f69d4a..339f4a0) is the immediately preceding commit\nthat introduced the getId()/getID() capitalization bug.\n"
